\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Translation between the angle spaces}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{For the constant scalar field of \ref{fdip-015W}, let #{X,Y} be its forward shifts using the inverse links on an oriented plane of #{V_0} sites. If its scalar flux is #{w}, then #{YX=\ue^{\ui\phi}XY} for #{\phi=2\pi w/V_0} by the oriented plaquette identity in \ref{fdip-01A6}. For #{v\in E_y}, multiplication by #{X} sends the eigenvalue equation to #{YXv=\ue^{\ui(y+\phi)}Xv}. Thus #{X^s} takes #{E_y} unitarily to #{E_{y+s\phi}}. In the [ordered evaluation](fdip-01C3), the weight of #{f_s(Y)X^s} at its output is #{f_s(y+s\phi)}.}
